# Site Adapter Rules

## New featured site

1. Class in `sites/<name>.py`
2. Register in `FEATURED_SITE_CLASSES` in `sites/__init__.py`
3. Add `tests/test_<name>.py` with mocked HTML fixtures
4. Update README supported-sites table (when user-facing)

## Required methods

- `validate_url(url)` — classmethod, registry lookup
- `is_url_vaildate()` — instance check after resolve (**keep typo**)
- Download entry via `start_download()` or site-specific path

## Patterns

- HLS → extend `M3U8Crawler` in `base.py`
- Direct MP4 → follow `direct_mp4.py` / `spankbang.py` / `hanime1.py`
- Multi-server embeds → mirror fallback like `javguru.py`
- Legacy URL-only → `sites/legacy/`, not featured list

## Workers & network

- MissAV: respect auto worker caps
- SupJav / Hanime1: max 4 ranged connections
- Headers from `core.config` — never hardcode user cookies/tokens
- Use `curl_cffi` when available (see `base.py` import pattern)

## Tests

- Mock page HTML — no live HTTP in unit tests
- Assert `validate_url`, key parse paths, stream URL extraction
- Site CDN changes are common — regression tests are mandatory
